    [1,'meaning','语境','If a question implies that someone lied, it _____ that accusation indirectly.',['suggests','proves with certainty','copies'],'suggests','第一义项是间接暗示。'],[2,'meaning','语境','“Rights imply duties” means that having rights _____ duties.',['involves or brings with it','is unrelated to','makes duties imaginary'],'involves or brings with it','第二义项表示某种结果或条件所意味着的内容。'],[3,'meaning','逻辑','If premise A implies conclusion B, B follows from A as a logical _____.',['consequence','imitation','illness'],'consequence','第三义项是逻辑上蕴含。'],[1,'distinction','辨析','A speaker may imply a point; the listener may ____ it.',['infer','implement','impede'],'infer','imply 是说话者暗示，infer 是听者推断。']
